            <p>
                Under this assumption, we compute <md> Z^* = 1.96 \ \text{and} \ SE \approx 0.095. </md> Hence, the confidence interval is <m>[0.71,1.09]</m>. Remember this means: assuming <m>H_0</m> is true, a random sample will produce a proportion between 90.5% and 99.5% 95% of the time. Since our sample falls within this range, it means that our sample is NOT UN-likely to occur. Show rejection region on the bell curve. 
            </p>

            <p>
                Since our sample proportion falls within the confidence interval, we do not have sufficient evidence to suggest the null hypothesis. It is NOT UN-likely that 9 in 10 dentists prefer Sensodyne. 
